  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indian government has scheduled a special session of Parliament to address proposed changes to legislative representation. The Union Cabinet recently finalized amendments to the Constitution Amendment Bill, which seeks to implement a 50 percent increase in Lok Sabha seats alongside a women's reservation provision. These legislative efforts aim to balance population-based representation with the interests of states that have achieved population stabilisation. While the ruling coalition maintains confidence in securing the necessary support, the process has faced scrutiny. Opposition leaders have criticized the government for not sharing the specific details of the bills with members of Parliament prior to the session. Political parties, including the DMK and NCP(SP), have indicated their intention to back the measures, though some have specified conditions regarding regional seat allocations and further internal review by party leadership.",
